#X text 240 83 inspired by Paul Bourke \, implementation by André Sier;
#X text 240 108 ---;
#X text 240 133 lyapunov random attractors;
#X text 240 158 ---;
#X text 240 183 Paul Bourke's words http://astronomy.swin.edu.au/%7Epbourke/fractals/lyapunov/;
#X text 240 223 ---;
#X text 240 248 On average 98% of the random selections of (an \, bn)
result in an infinite series.;
#X text 240 288 This is so common because of the range (-2<=a \, b<=2)
for each of the parameters a and b \, the number of infinite cases
will reduce greatly with a smaller range.;
#X text 240 343 About 1% were point attractors \, and about 0.5% were
periodic basins of attraction.;
#X text 240 383 ===;
#X text 240 408 x[n+1] = a[0] + a[1]*x[n] + a[2]*x[n]^2 + a[3]*x[n]*y[n]
+ a[4]*y[n] + a[5]*y[n]^2;
#X text 240 448 y[n+1] = b[0] + b[1]*x[n] + b[2]*x[n]^2 + b[3]*x[n]*y[n]
+ b[4]*y[n] + b[5]*y[n]^2;
#X text 240 488 ===;
